### t=4 spin 9 ###
  k(t0+eps) = 2*(-eps - 3)/(eps + 1)
  = -6 + 4*eps - 4*eps**2 + O(eps**3)
  n(t0+eps) = (-eps - 9)/(eps + 1)
  M(t0+eps) = (-eps - 1)/(2*(eps + 3))

  EXACT LIMIT STATEMENT:
  For t = 4 + eps, eps -> 0+:
    monic(WKB_charge_9(t)) = cert_9(t)  [EXACT, for all rational t in a neighbourhood]
    Therefore: lim_{eps->0} monic(WKB_charge_9(4+eps))
             = lim_{eps->0} cert_9(4+eps)
             = cert_9(4)  [by continuity of the rational function cert_9(t)]
  cert_9(4) has 21 terms (computed above).
  cert(4+1/100) - cert(4): 20 terms (O(1/100) as expected)

